  {
    "type": "tweet",
    "id": "2058226726728016037",
    "url": "https://x.com/Trader_XO/status/2058226726728016037",
    "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/Trader_XO/status/2058226726728016037",
    "text": "I think the short around 81.5 was readable from a price action pov, there was enough structure/rejection to build a case for it, but personally I'd have felt as though I'm just guessing, not playing an actual probability vs the conviction, timing and confidence I get from profile and flow - (my own performance over the last few years tells me that)..\n\nThat said, I mainly use orderflow for futures/perps, where the venue level auction tends to be cleaner and more actionable. \n\nWith equities etc.., I only use volume and market profile, not so much orderflow as in footprints etc because my approach is more momentum based, and equity flow is fragmented across venues, dark pools, various data feeds..\n\nPersonally volume profile and orderflow don\u2019t replace price action, they add context/confluence around it.\n\nPrice action gives me the setup -  profile/orderflow helps refine execution, invalidation, and conviction.\n\nIf I were starting again, I\u2019d learn pure price action and volume first. Structure, liquidity, acceptance/rejection, failed auctions, range behaviour, trend days, etc. \n\nOnly after that orderflow. Otherwise it\u2019s easy to get lost in the approach without understanding what price is actually doing.\n\nJust to add that a trade setup isnt a strategy, but a strategy contains a given trade setup and many other facets of a trade, risk, position sizing etc - how you structure the trade... excuse the typos - grammar",
    "source": "Twitter Web App",
